#. Tag: title
#: getting-online.docbook:2
#, no-c-format
msgid "Getting online the easy way"
msgstr "Jednostavan način za spajanje na mrežu"

#. Tag: title
#: getting-online.docbook:5
#, no-c-format
msgid "A few things you should have ready before you start"
msgstr "Nekoliko stvari koje bi trebali spremiti prije nego počnete"

#. Tag: para
#: getting-online.docbook:7
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have a fairly modern &Linux; distribution, you might find the rest of "
"this document superfluous. &kppp; comes with a clever little wizard that in "
"many cases can have you up and running with an internet connection in just a "
"few minutes."
msgstr ""
"Ukoliko posjedujete dovoljno dobru &Linux; distribuciju, mogli biste ostatak "
"ovog dokumenta smatrati suvišnim. &kppp; dolazi u kombinaciji sa pametnim "
"malim čarobnjakom, kako biste za nekoliko minuta mogli postaviti internet "
"konekciju."

#. Tag: para
#: getting-online.docbook:12
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Whether using the wizard or not, you should know the following information "
"before you begin:"
msgstr ""
"Prije nego počnete, svejedno da li koristite ili ne koristite čarobnjak, "
"sljedećih nekoliko informacija biste trebali znati:"

#. Tag: para
#: getting-online.docbook:16
#, no-c-format
msgid "Your <acronym>ISP</acronym> modem pool phone number."
msgstr "Broj telefona skupa modema od vašeg <acronym>ISP</acronym>."

#. Tag: para
#: getting-online.docbook:18
#, no-c-format
msgid "Your username and password for your <acronym>ISP</acronym>."
msgstr "Korisničko ime i šifra za Vaš <acronym>ISP</acronym>."

#. Tag: para
#: getting-online.docbook:20
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Your <acronym>ISP</acronym>'s <acronym>DNS</acronym> servers (one is "
"sufficient, but two is better)."
msgstr ""
"Vaši <acronym>ISP</acronym> <acronym>DNS</acronym> serveri (jedan je "
"dovoljan, ali dva je bolje)."

#. Tag: para
#: getting-online.docbook:24
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Other optional information you should find out to fully access your "
"<acronym>ISP</acronym>'s services are:"
msgstr ""
"Ostale neobavezne informacije koje biste trebali saznati kako biste u "
"potpunosti pristupili Vašim  <acronym>ISP</acronym> servisima su:"

#. Tag: para
#: getting-online.docbook:28
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The incoming mail server address (often <systemitem class=\"systemname\">pop."
"yourisp.com</systemitem> or <systemitem class=\"systemname\">mail.yourisp."
"com</systemitem>)"
msgstr ""
"Dolazna adresa mail servera (često <systemitem class=\"systemname\">pop."
"yourisp.com</systemitem> ili <systemitem class=\"systemname\">mail.yourisp."
"com</systemitem>)"

#. Tag: para
#: getting-online.docbook:30
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Also find out if your <acronym>ISP</acronym> uses the POP3 protocol or IMAP."
msgstr ""
"Također saznajte ukoliko Vaš <acronym>ISP</acronym> koristi POP3 protokol "
"ili IMAP."

#. Tag: para
#: getting-online.docbook:32
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The outgoing (<acronym>SMTP</acronym>) mail server address (it could be the "
"same as the incoming mail server, or it is often called something like "
"<systemitem class=\"systemname\">smtp.yourisp.com</systemitem>)."
msgstr ""
"Odlazna (<acronym>SMTP</acronym>) adresa mail servera (mogla bi biti ista "
"kao dolazni mail server, ili se često naziva <systemitem class=\"systemname"
"\">smtp.yourisp.com</systemitem>)."

#. Tag: para
#: getting-online.docbook:36
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Usenet News (<acronym>NNTP</acronym>) server address (possibly "
"<systemitem class=\"systemname\">news.yourisp.com</systemitem> or "
"<systemitem class=\"systemname\">nntp.yourisp.com</systemitem>)."
msgstr ""
"Usenet News (<acronym>NNTP</acronym>) server adresa (možda <systemitem class="
"\"systemname\">news.yourisp.com</systemitem> ili <systemitem class="
"\"systemname\">nntp.yourisp.com</systemitem>)."

#. Tag: para
#: getting-online.docbook:39
#, no-c-format
msgid "Any proxy servers your <acronym>ISP</acronym> has set up."
msgstr "BIlo koji proxy server koga je <acronym>ISP</acronym> postavio."

#. Tag: para
#: getting-online.docbook:43
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All this information is probably available on any paperwork you received "
"from your <acronym>ISP</acronym> when you signed up with them, or you can "
"find it out from your <acronym>ISP</acronym>'s support telephone line."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: getting-online.docbook:47
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Armed with the above, and a fairly recent default installation of &Linux;, "
"you may well find that setting up an internet connection is as simple as "
"running the &kppp; wizard."
msgstr ""
